      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, my electric water heater is making this really loud knocking sound every now and then and the water isnt staying hot anymore. any idea what it could be or do i just need to call a plumber?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A loud knocking sound from your electric water heater, combined with the water not staying hot, could be due to a few reasons. It might be a sign that the heating element is failing, or there could be sediment buildup causing the knocking sound. You could try running a hot water cycle to see if it helps, but if the problem persists, it might be time to call a plumber. However, if you're feeling adventurous, you could also try inspecting the tank for any signs of damage or leaks. Just be careful, as working with an electric water heater can be dangerous. If you do decide to inspect it yourself, make sure to turn off the power to the unit first. And remember, if you encounter any stubborn issues, it's always best to call a professional. They might even have a few handy tips or tricks up their sleeve to help you out. After all, a plumber is like a trusty sidekick in the battle against pesky water heater problems. But if you're feeling brave, you could always try to tackle it yourself. Just remember, with great power comes great responsibility, and in this case, great responsibility means not turning your water heater into a mini volcano. Good luck, and may the spirits of the water heater gods be with you",
